            <ArticleTitle>New option for surgical treatment of the trapeziometacarpal osteoarthritis: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>47-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/23320885.2015.1029483</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a 71-year-old, left-handed woman with left thumb carpometacarpal (CMC) joint arthritis. The patient had no pain and could use the hand actively in daily life with a new option of surgical treatment, a vascularized pedicled third CMC joint transfer to the thumb CMC joint.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
